# SHA-256 of every raw llama-server log and GPU telemetry trace behind this
# repository's controlled tier. 702 logs and 19 traces, 4071 MB uncompressed.
#
# The logs are not committed - 4 GB against a 90 MB repository - so this is what
# ties the committed JSON to the files it was derived from. Each attested run
# also records `server_log_sha256` per arm-run in its own arm-run JSON, so a
# single log can be checked without this file.
#
# Paths are relative to the benchmark host's ~/bench.
# Produced by: bash bench/collect_evidence.sh ~/bench
#
# The archive of those files:
#   raw_logs.tar.zst   271 028 599 bytes (259 MiB), zstd -19
#   sha256             29c2401f100390268bbd52e43b5c2da9a61440bad3dabe502ca1684478771fd6
#
# Published 2026-08-27 as the release asset `raw-evidence-2026-08-27`, with the
# 19 telemetry traces beside it. Committed hashes tie the derived JSON to files
# nobody else can see; publishing is what lets the extraction be re-run instead
# of trusted. `.github/workflows/evidence.yml` re-runs it: 12 of 12 records of
# spec_accounting_20260826.json, 12 of 12 of checkpoint_timers_20260826.json and
# 526 of the 535 rows of acceptance_counter_comparison.json come back identical,
# none differing. The nine are runs G, I and J, whose logs are in the archive
# and whose arm-run JSON is not committed because those runs never completed
# their cell set - see v4_audit_2026_08_25/README.md.
#
